{"answer": "Implemented FB_Task for SELF008 and compiled successfully with the CODESYS compiler (0 errors, 0 warnings).

Declaration:
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
    Request : BOOL;
    Trip : BOOL;
    Preset : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    Ready : BOOL;
    Count : USINT;
END_VAR

Implementation:
IF Trip OR NOT Request OR (Preset < USINT#1) OR (Preset > USINT#5) THEN
    Count := USINT#0;
    Ready := FALSE;
ELSE
    IF Count < Preset THEN
        Count := Count + USINT#1;
    END_IF
    Ready := (Count >= Preset);
END_IF

Behavior: Trip / missing Request / Preset outside 1..5 immediately clear Count and Ready (highest priority); otherwise the count increments and saturates at Preset, with Ready asserted exactly when Count reaches Preset. Preset changes apply within the same scan (e.g., Preset 5 with Count 1 → Preset 1 yields Count 1, Ready TRUE). Outputs are assigned every scan so the initial conditions (Count=0, Ready=FALSE) persist until a valid healthy scan. Note: only compilation was verified; no PLC functional/online tests were executed."}

